    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118-a4">

                <pb facs="0244" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg150"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 99.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gadeke to Mr. Kickbusch.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consular Agency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Konigsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: In compliance with the request of the
                    United States embassy at Berlin of June 10, instant, to report upon the tonnage
                    dues and other taxes imposed since January 26, 1888, upon American vessels
                    arrived here, I beg to inform you that no American vessels have entered this
                    port for more than fifteen years, the whole time I have been in charge.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conrad H. Gadeke</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consular
                    Agency.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
